# Reward Triage — Master Context

**Goal.** Build a host-agnostic Reward Triage component. Given N LLM-written reward functions for an RL task, it drops weak candidates before expensive PPO training so only the top-k get full runs. Hosts (EvoNav, EUREKA or CARD style loops) call it; it never depends on a host. This repo has exactly three environments: native 2D, CrowdNav++ and IR-SIM. HighwayEnv is not part of it. The host is not chosen yet: this plan only makes the component integration-ready; no external host is wired in.

**Design decision (2026-11-11).** Every environment produces its own labels during the pipeline run itself; there is no pre-collected per-environment dataset and no transfer between environments. Target: online reward search — reach the same success as a train-all loop with fewer PPO steps, learning only from labels the run itself produces.

**Established facts.**

- 2D env `RewardNavigation2D-v0`; 108 parametric rewards (12 families x 3 seeds, 50k PPO steps); six fixed components (progress, goal, collision, obstacle, smoothness, time) with weights.
- Primary protocol: leave-one-family-out (LOFO), inner LOFO for hyperparameters, family one-hot disabled.
- Pre-registered confirm result (ExtraTrees, `early+math`, success_rate): pooled Spearman 0.933, within-family Spearman 0.616 (std 0.453), within-family top-3 hit 0.722. The operating feature set `early+math+behavioral` (0.935 / 0.648 / 0.833) was chosen after seeing the exploratory grid. Report both. The confirm `run_config.json` records git_commit 2fb024c, not HEAD.
- Both feature sets use `early_*` features, recorded in config as 12,000 PPO steps per candidate. Zero-PPO-cost sets (`math`, `behavioral`, `math+behavioral`) have no results in tracked artifacts (`oof_predictions.csv` holds only 4 model x feature_set combos).
- About 64% of label variance is between families, so pooled Spearman is inflated. The host use case is ranking inside one generation (about 16 similar candidates), so within-group and pool-level metrics are primary.
- Label noise: median seed std about 0.023; about 25% of within-family pairs differ by less than 1 standard error (3 seeds).
- CrowdNav++ campaigns: v1_50k, v4_full_150k (72 pool, robot visible), v5_invisible_24 (24 pool, robot_visible=false, only 2 per family: use top-1 and pairwise). IR-SIM campaign v1_nav24 (24 pool = 12x2, PPO 50k, early 2k/5k/12k) has the same n=2 limitation. Backends via `scripts/run_quality_pipeline.py --env 2d|crowdnav|irsim`.
- Package is `rsr`. Locked confirm artifacts must not be rewritten.
- Phase 3.5 done: default feature group `mb`; container runner (Docker); sizing in `docs/phase4_sizing.md`.

**Runtime choices (2026-11-11).**

- LLM: xAI, model `grok-4.3` (VERIFY exact API model id in Phase 4 client).
- Isolation: Docker (`Dockerfile.triage` / `docker-compose.triage.yml`).
- Compute budget (agent default): 4 workers; G=5 gens; N=16; 3 seeds. **One env at a time** — finish 2D (including its repeated runs and result review), then start CrowdNav++ or IR-SIM from scratch only after the user says so. Never auto-chain all envs. See `docs/phase4_sizing.md`.

**Global rules (every phase).**

1. Follow `.cursor/rules/token-efficiency.mdc`: read only files named in the phase, no repo-wide scans, localized edits.
2. Never modify locked artifacts: `experiments/model_comparison_confirm/`, `results/model_comparison_confirm/`, `experiments/archives/`, `docs/archive/`. Every new experiment gets a new run_id and its own directories. Writer scripts refuse a non-empty output dir without `--force`.
3. English only for code comments, logs, prints, docstrings and commit messages.
4. No new PPO runs unless a phase says so. Never launch jobs longer than 10 minutes; print the command and provide `--dry-run` and `--max-jobs 1` pilots.
5. Evaluation discipline: group-held-out CV only; preprocessing and hyperparameter search fit on train folds only; keep the existing leakage asserts; success, collision and timeout stay separate (no scalar fitness); report negative results.
6. Pre-register: before any confirmatory run, commit `docs/prereg/<phase>.md`. Anything chosen after seeing results is labeled exploratory.
7. Each phase ends with `pytest -m 'not slow'` green, `docs/phase_reports/phase_N.md`, and one commit per logical step prefixed `phaseN:`.
8. Keep existing CLI scripts working (thin wrappers) and existing results reproducible.

**Gates.** Stop after Phase 2 (done: Gate 1 CONDITIONAL), Phase 6 (Gate 2), and Phase 7 (Gate 3); write the gate report and wait. No Gate 1b / no cross-env transfer.

**Envs.** Only 2D, CrowdNav++, IR-SIM. No HighwayEnv. External host wiring deferred until after Gate 3.
